<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">County Donegal</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Donegal, Tír Chonaill</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">County Donegal is a county in the north-west of Ireland, part of the province of Ulster but in the Republic of Ireland. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it was largely the lordship of Tír Chonaill, ruled by the O'Donnells, whose leaders took part in the Flight of the Earls from Rathmullan in 1607. Its rugged Atlantic coast includes some of the highest sea cliffs in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/county-donegal.jpg" alt="County Donegal" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Island_of_Ireland_location_map.svg: *Ireland_location_map.svg: NordNordWest Northern_Ireland_location_map.svg: NordNo... · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Island_of_Ireland_location_map_Donegal.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
